In article <1991Dec18.180346.29035@cbnewsl.cb.att.com> wjb@moss.ATT.COM writes:
>Why is it that the same login playing the same character by the same
>name can appear several times in the score file, particularly, several
>times in the top ten list?

There is an option in the game of nethack which is set at compile time, which
allows the game compiler to determine how many times each player can be on
the high score list.  This sounds like your games administrator (or the person
who compiled the game) set that number rather high, which allows people to
have multiple high scores.

